# Cloudflare Pages: headers for every page and file of asklocker.com.
# No other site may show AskLocker inside a frame, so a hidden frame cannot
# trick someone into tapping Accept or Delete. No plug-in content and no
# <base> pointing elsewhere (074). Which scripts may run is not limited yet:
# Google's, Razorpay's and the readers from jsDelivr need a list tried in a
# browser first (docs/end-to-end-encryption.md, Phase 5).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# The DEV-only test pages (dist/lab/, removed from every other build by
# scripts/lab-pages.mjs) run the search model on several threads, which a
# browser allows only on a cross-origin isolated page. Never the app's
# pages: isolation would break Google's and Razorpay's windows.
/lab/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
